<title>CANADA: WCE canola/grain pre-opening calls.</title>
<headline>WCE canola/grain pre-opening calls.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Winnipeg Commodity Exchange canola and grain futures pre-opening call as of 0820 CDT.</p>
<p>CANOLA - Mixed. C$1.00 a tonne lower to C$1.00 higher as traders watch the open on the CBOT soycomplex and weekend weather forecasts for the U.S. Midwest. November WCE canola crush profit margins fell to -6.06 Wednesday from -1.59 Tuesday. Canada's dollar opened firm at C$1.3731, rose to 84.54 yen and rose to 1.3069 marks.</p>
<p>FLAXSEED - Steady.</p>
<p>WESTERN BARLEY - Steady, watching U.S. markets and weekend weather forecasts.</p>
<p>FEED WHEAT - Steady.</p>
<p>PEAS - Steady.</p>
<p>OATS - Steady.</p>
<p>(All values in Canadian dollars/tonne except peas, oats)</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
